WEBVTT

00:00:15.288 --> 00:00:45.356
Tails from the Thousand and One Nights Copyright Black Cat Publishing The story of Sharaya and Sharazad, his vizier's daughter.

00:00:45.416 --> 00:00:54.612
Part 1 There were once two kings called Sharaya and Shahzaman.

00:00:54.672 --> 00:00:56.552
They were brothers.

00:00:56.612 --> 00:00:59.504
Shahraya was an important king.

00:00:59.564 --> 00:01:03.937
He ruled all of Persia, India and China.

00:01:03.997 --> 00:01:09.444
Shahzaman, his younger brother, was the king of Samarkand.

00:01:09.504 --> 00:01:19.921
One day, Sharaya said to his vizier, I'd like to see my brother, go to his palace in Samarkand and invite him to India.

00:01:19.981 --> 00:01:28.844
The vizier, who had two daughters, Sharazad and Dinazad, made preparations for his long journey.

00:01:28.904 --> 00:01:32.835
He and his servants travelled day and night.

00:01:32.895 --> 00:01:38.796
When they arrived in Samarkand, the king greeted the vizier warmly.

00:01:38.856 --> 00:01:41.566
Welcome to Samarkand.

00:01:41.626 --> 00:01:42.576
He said.

00:01:42.636 --> 00:01:45.328
Tell me, how is my brother?

00:01:45.388 --> 00:01:50.032
He is well your majesty, but he'd like to see you again.

00:01:50.092 --> 00:01:52.384
He told me to invite you to India.

00:01:52.444 --> 00:01:54.917
I'll prepare for the journey immediately.

00:01:54.977 --> 00:01:55.908
Said the king.

00:01:55.968 --> 00:02:01.062
You and your servants can put your tents in the big field outside the city walls.

00:02:01.122 --> 00:02:03.064
Wait for me there.

00:02:03.124 --> 00:02:09.023
One evening, ten days later, Shahzaman arrived at the viziers camp.

00:02:09.083 --> 00:02:15.669
We'll start our journey early tomorrow morning," he told the Visier, and then he went to bed.

00:02:15.729 --> 00:02:19.920
At midnight, the Visier received a visit from the king.

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:24.941
I'd like to say goodbye to my wife one more time, he said.

00:02:25.001 --> 00:02:27.462
I'm going to return to the city.

00:02:27.522 --> 00:02:34.193
Shah Zaman rode back to the palace and went straight to his wife's bedroom and opened the door.

00:02:34.253 --> 00:02:38.752
She was there in bed, but she wasn't alone.

00:02:38.812 --> 00:02:41.642
She was with one of the kitchen boys.

00:02:41.701 --> 00:02:44.684
Shah Zaman was very angry.

00:02:44.743 --> 00:02:48.516
He took out his sword and killed both of them.

00:02:48.576 --> 00:02:51.359
Then he returned to the camp.

00:02:51.418 --> 00:02:58.524
The next day, the king, the vizier, and all their servants left Samakhand.

00:02:58.584 --> 00:03:01.906
They traveled for many days and nights.

00:03:01.966 --> 00:03:06.020
Finally, they arrived at the Royal Palace in India.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:09.534
Sharaya came out to greet his brother.

00:03:09.594 --> 00:03:12.386
He was very happy to see him again.

00:03:12.446 --> 00:03:16.358
He gave him clean clothes, food, and drink.

00:03:16.418 --> 00:03:18.689
He gave him a palace to stay in.

00:03:18.749 --> 00:03:25.632
That palace will be your home here, he said, but you must come and see me every day.

00:03:25.692 --> 00:03:29.404
The two brothers spent the days pleasantly.

00:03:29.464 --> 00:03:33.811
They talked, played chess, and walked in the gardens.

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:38.056
but Shah Zaman thought about his wife all the time.

00:03:38.116 --> 00:03:40.206
He was very sad.

00:03:40.266 --> 00:03:41.858
He stopped eating.

00:03:41.918 --> 00:03:44.338
He became thin and pale.

00:03:44.398 --> 00:03:46.219
His brother was worried.

00:03:46.279 --> 00:03:49.271
Perhaps he wants to go home, he thought.

00:03:49.331 --> 00:03:51.782
I'll send him back soon.

00:03:51.842 --> 00:03:57.434
One morning, Shahriya said, I'm going hunting in the forest, brother.

00:03:57.494 --> 00:03:59.836
I'll be away for 10 days.

00:03:59.896 --> 00:04:03.560
Would you like to come with me before you go back to Samarkand?

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:06.434
Thank you, brother, but I'm tired.

00:04:06.494 --> 00:04:07.495
You go.

00:04:07.555 --> 00:04:08.806
I'll stay here."

00:04:08.866 --> 00:04:11.276
replied Shahzaman.

00:04:11.336 --> 00:04:15.398
He sat at his bedroom window all day.

00:04:15.458 --> 00:04:18.781
He thought about his wife and felt sad.

00:04:18.841 --> 00:04:22.852
He could see the garden of his brother's palace from his window.

00:04:22.912 --> 00:04:24.923
It was very beautiful.

00:04:24.983 --> 00:04:27.374
There were trees and flowers.

00:04:27.434 --> 00:04:29.166
There were peacocks.

00:04:29.225 --> 00:04:31.119
There was a fountain.

00:04:31.179 --> 00:04:36.985
There were also two people in the garden that day, a man and a woman.

00:04:37.045 --> 00:04:39.496
They were kissing and laughing.

00:04:39.556 --> 00:04:42.358
Shahazaman looked at them carefully.

00:04:42.418 --> 00:04:48.301
The woman was his brother's wife, and the man was one of her slaves.

00:04:48.361 --> 00:04:51.572
Shahazaman was very surprised.

00:04:51.632 --> 00:04:58.576
He thought, my brother's more important than me, but he's unlucky with his wife too.

00:04:58.636 --> 00:05:01.202
And he began to feel better.

00:05:01.262 --> 00:05:05.008
He started eating again.

00:05:05.068 --> 00:05:16.689
Part 2 When Sharaya came back from hunting and saw his brother, he said, You are well now, brother.

00:05:16.748 --> 00:05:18.090
I am happy.

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:21.812
Tell me, why were you so sad before?

00:05:21.872 --> 00:05:26.367
Shah Zaman told him about his own wife and the kitchen boy.

00:05:26.426 --> 00:05:31.146
Then he told Sharaya about his wife and her slave.

00:05:31.206 --> 00:05:34.423
Sharaya loved his wife very much.

00:05:34.483 --> 00:05:37.474
He said, I don't believe you.

00:05:37.534 --> 00:05:40.216
My wife's a good woman.

00:05:40.275 --> 00:05:43.777
Go hunting again tomorrow, said his brother.

00:05:43.837 --> 00:05:46.728
But come back secretly in the evening.

00:05:46.788 --> 00:05:48.999
Then you'll see them.

00:05:49.059 --> 00:05:53.641
So the next day, Sharaya went to the forest.

00:05:53.701 --> 00:05:57.215
When it was dark, he returned on foot.

00:05:57.275 --> 00:06:03.052
In the morning, the king went to his brother's room and looked down into the garden.

00:06:03.112 --> 00:06:05.874
His wife and her slave were there.

00:06:05.934 --> 00:06:08.416
They were kissing and laughing.

00:06:08.476 --> 00:06:10.938
Shariah was very angry.

00:06:10.998 --> 00:06:13.251
He immediately called his vizier.

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:15.412
Kill them both, he said.

00:06:15.472 --> 00:06:17.024
Oh, brother.

00:06:17.083 --> 00:06:18.605
Said Shahzaman.

00:06:18.665 --> 00:06:21.387
There are no good women in the world.

00:06:21.447 --> 00:06:23.298
They are all bad.

00:06:23.358 --> 00:06:25.391
You are right, brother.

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:28.218
The king replied sadly.

00:06:28.278 --> 00:06:33.927
Soon after this, Shahzaman went back to Samarkand.

00:06:33.986 --> 00:06:43.010
One night, a month or two later, Shahraya said to his vizier, I want a new wife, go and find one for me.

00:06:43.070 --> 00:06:45.390
The vizier found a girl.

00:06:45.450 --> 00:06:49.872
He took her to the king's bedroom, and Shahraya married her.

00:06:49.932 --> 00:06:55.000
In the morning, he said to his vizier, now kill her.

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:59.778
The next night, he told his vizier to find him another girl.

00:06:59.838 --> 00:07:03.700
The vizier found one, and Sharaya married her.

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:07.332
In the morning, he told his vizier to kill her.

00:07:07.391 --> 00:07:14.256
Every night, the king married a different girl, and in the morning, his vizier killed her.

00:07:14.316 --> 00:07:17.867
The people in the kingdom became very angry with the king.

00:07:17.927 --> 00:07:21.028
They didn't like losing their daughters.

00:07:21.088 --> 00:07:28.439
One day, Sharazad, the vizier's daughter said, Father, I'd like to marry the king.

00:07:28.499 --> 00:07:31.692
I want to try to help our people."

00:07:31.751 --> 00:07:34.664
She was a very intelligent girl.

00:07:34.724 --> 00:07:38.396
She read and studied a lot and knew many things.

00:07:38.456 --> 00:07:42.900
But when her father heard this, he was angry, his silly girl.

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:48.585
The king will spend one night with you, and then, in the morning, I'll have to kill you.

00:07:48.644 --> 00:07:51.777
I want to help our people, Father.

00:07:51.837 --> 00:07:53.446
Shahazad said.

00:07:53.506 --> 00:07:55.024
I have a plan.

00:07:55.084 --> 00:07:57.676
Please, take me to the king."

00:07:57.736 --> 00:08:01.720
The Visier was sad, but he took her to the king.

00:08:01.780 --> 00:08:08.054
Later that night, when the king and Sharazad were in bed, she started crying.

00:08:08.114 --> 00:08:09.716
Why are you crying?

00:08:09.775 --> 00:08:11.617
asked the king.

00:08:11.677 --> 00:08:17.927
I'd like to see my sister one more time before I die, she said.

00:08:17.986 --> 00:08:22.224
So the king sent for her sister, Dinazad.

00:08:22.284 --> 00:08:30.661
When she arrived, she went and sat next to Shahrazad and said, Sister, tell me a story please.

00:08:30.721 --> 00:08:33.254
The night will pass more pleasantly.

00:08:33.314 --> 00:08:36.606
Shahrazad began to tell a story.

00:08:36.667 --> 00:08:38.808
Dinazad listened.

00:08:38.868 --> 00:08:42.952
The king wasn't tired, so he listened too.

00:08:43.011 --> 00:08:47.316
She told one story and started another one.

00:08:47.376 --> 00:08:52.590
But when she saw the first light of mourning through the window, she stopped.

00:08:52.650 --> 00:08:56.234
"'I must know the end of that story,' said the king.

00:08:56.254 --> 00:08:58.456
"'You must finish it tomorrow.'"

00:08:58.516 --> 00:09:02.670
So her father didn't have to kill her in the morning.

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:08.704
The next night, Shahazad finished the story and started another one.

00:09:08.764 --> 00:09:14.900
She continued to tell the king's stories for one thousand and one nights.

00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:18.742
During this time, they had three children.

00:09:18.802 --> 00:09:25.664
Then one day, the king said, You are a good and intelligent woman, Sharad Zad.

00:09:25.724 --> 00:09:27.325
I will never kill you.

00:09:27.385 --> 00:09:29.596
You will be my queen."

00:09:29.656 --> 00:09:35.799
And they lived happily together for the rest of their lives.

00:09:35.859 --> 00:09:47.445
The Enchanted Horse Part 1 It was new year in the city of Shiraz in Persia.

00:09:47.505 --> 00:09:50.236
The city square was full of people.

00:09:50.296 --> 00:09:53.137
The king and his family were there too.

00:09:53.197 --> 00:09:55.798
There was music and dancing.

00:09:55.858 --> 00:09:59.008
There were fire eaters and snake charmers.

00:09:59.068 --> 00:10:03.890
And of course, there was a lot of delicious food and drink.

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:08.462
Suddenly, an Indian man appeared in front of the king.

00:10:08.522 --> 00:10:11.302
He had a beautiful horse with him.

00:10:11.362 --> 00:10:14.155
It was made of black wood.

00:10:14.215 --> 00:10:17.018
the Indian spoke to the king.

00:10:17.078 --> 00:10:22.329
Your Majesty, this is a very special horse.

00:10:22.389 --> 00:10:23.349
Really?

00:10:23.409 --> 00:10:24.410
Said the king.

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:25.960
Why is it special?

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:27.740
What can it do?

00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:30.751
It can fly your Majesty.

00:10:30.811 --> 00:10:38.028
When I press this little button on its neck, it flies up into the air and takes me where I want to go.

00:10:38.088 --> 00:10:42.915
Your horse is certainly a very special horse, said the king.

00:10:42.975 --> 00:10:45.206
I'd like to have it for myself.

00:10:45.266 --> 00:10:47.957
I'll sell it to you, your Majesty.

00:10:48.017 --> 00:10:49.868
And what's the price?

00:10:49.928 --> 00:10:51.258
Ask the king.

00:10:51.318 --> 00:10:53.219
Your daughter.

00:10:53.279 --> 00:10:55.870
I want to marry your daughter.

00:10:55.930 --> 00:10:57.571
Reply the Indian.

00:10:57.631 --> 00:11:00.432
That's a very high price for a horse.

00:11:00.492 --> 00:11:05.454
It isn't a high price for a horse that can fly your Majesty.

00:11:05.514 --> 00:11:08.678
Try it, and you'll see for yourself.

00:11:08.738 --> 00:11:14.054
Let my son, Prince Feroos, try the horse, said the king.

00:11:14.114 --> 00:11:20.898
Prince Feroos immediately jumped on the horse's back and pressed the button on its neck.

00:11:20.958 --> 00:11:26.442
The horse flew up into the air, into the clouds and disappeared.

00:11:26.502 --> 00:11:28.863
The king was very angry.

00:11:28.923 --> 00:11:30.074
Where is my son?

00:11:30.134 --> 00:11:32.386
He shouted, bring him back.

00:11:32.446 --> 00:11:33.596
I can't.

00:11:33.656 --> 00:11:35.448
replied the Indian.

00:11:35.508 --> 00:11:39.642
The king ordered his guards to put the Indian in prison.

00:11:39.702 --> 00:11:45.704
My guards will kill you if Prince Feroos isn't back in three months, he said.

00:11:45.764 --> 00:11:50.956
Meanwhile, the horse and the prince flew higher and higher.

00:11:51.016 --> 00:11:52.856
The prince was happy.

00:11:52.916 --> 00:11:55.758
He enjoyed flying on the horse.

00:11:55.818 --> 00:11:58.818
Then it began to get dark.

00:11:58.878 --> 00:12:00.970
It's late, he thought.

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:02.900
I must land.

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:08.274
He looked carefully at the horse's neck and saw another little button.

00:12:08.334 --> 00:12:14.628
He pressed it and the horse landed on the terrace of a beautiful white palace.

00:12:14.688 --> 00:12:17.920
He got off and looked around him.

00:12:17.980 --> 00:12:21.642
There was a small door in the corner of the terrace.

00:12:21.702 --> 00:12:24.814
He opened it and saw some stairs.

00:12:24.874 --> 00:12:29.418
He went down them and into a long hall with many doors.

00:12:29.478 --> 00:12:34.072
There was a light under one of them, so he opened it.

00:12:34.132 --> 00:12:37.546
Six guards were asleep on the floor.

00:12:37.606 --> 00:12:42.808
The light was coming from a lamp in another room behind a curtain.

00:12:42.868 --> 00:12:47.638
Prince Farus moved the curtain and looked in.

00:12:47.698 --> 00:12:52.930
He saw a big sofa and some women asleep around it.

00:12:52.990 --> 00:12:57.252
On the sofa there was a very beautiful girl.

00:12:57.312 --> 00:13:03.051
Prince Farus touched her arm gently and she opened her eyes.

00:13:03.111 --> 00:13:05.430
Don't be afraid, he said.

00:13:05.490 --> 00:13:08.051
I'm the son of the king of Persia.

00:13:08.111 --> 00:13:09.752
I don't want to hurt you.

00:13:09.812 --> 00:13:12.553
I'm lost and in danger.

00:13:12.613 --> 00:13:17.045
I'm the daughter of the Sultan of Bengal, said the princess.

00:13:17.105 --> 00:13:18.176
Don't worry.

00:13:18.236 --> 00:13:20.386
You're safe in my palace.

00:13:20.446 --> 00:13:26.729
Then she called one of her maids and said to her, Give the prince some food and a bed.

00:13:26.789 --> 00:13:28.790
We'll talk in the morning.

00:13:28.850 --> 00:13:33.714
The princess thought about the handsome young prince all night.

00:13:33.774 --> 00:13:41.172
The next morning she put on her most beautiful dress and finest jewels and went out into the garden.

00:13:41.232 --> 00:13:43.693
Prince Farus was there.

00:13:43.753 --> 00:13:46.064
He told her his story.

00:13:46.124 --> 00:13:50.828
Dear Princess, I must return home to my father, he said.

00:13:50.888 --> 00:13:53.369
He doesn't know that I'm here.

00:13:53.429 --> 00:13:56.602
The Princess was sad when she heard this.

00:13:56.662 --> 00:13:59.605
Can't you stay for just two more days?

00:13:59.665 --> 00:14:00.495
She asked.

00:14:00.555 --> 00:14:02.076
I'm lonely here.

00:14:02.136 --> 00:14:06.358
My maids and the palace guards are my only companions.

00:14:06.418 --> 00:14:15.422
The prince looked at the sad face of the beautiful princess of Bengal and decided to stay.

00:14:15.482 --> 00:14:19.433
Part two.

00:14:19.493 --> 00:14:24.526
The days became weeks and the weeks became months.

00:14:24.586 --> 00:14:27.568
The prince and the princess fell in love.

00:14:27.628 --> 00:14:29.678
They wanted to get married.

00:14:29.738 --> 00:14:34.319
One day, Prince Varus said, I must go back to Persia.

00:14:34.379 --> 00:14:36.569
My father's waiting for me.

00:14:36.629 --> 00:14:37.920
Come with me.

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:40.770
We can get married and live there.

00:14:40.830 --> 00:14:43.041
The princess agreed.

00:14:43.101 --> 00:14:50.362
So that night after dark, they both got on the horses back and flew across the skies to Persia.

00:14:50.422 --> 00:14:54.734
They landed in the garden of a small house outside the city.

00:14:54.794 --> 00:14:59.546
Stay here tonight, he told her, I'll come for you tomorrow.

00:14:59.606 --> 00:15:03.778
Then Prince Faroos went to his father's palace.

00:15:03.838 --> 00:15:07.940
The king was very happy to see his son again.

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:10.910
He told the guards to bring the Indian to him.

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:16.082
Take your horse and never enter my kingdom again, he said to him.

00:15:16.142 --> 00:15:20.624
The Indian was angry with the king because he put him in prison.

00:15:20.684 --> 00:15:24.879
And he was angry with Prince Faroos because he took his horse.

00:15:24.939 --> 00:15:27.674
He wanted his revenge.

00:15:27.734 --> 00:15:35.640
The palace guards told the Indian that his horse was in a house outside the city, so he went there the next day.

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:38.302
A servant answered the door.

00:15:38.362 --> 00:15:43.106
The Indian said, The prince is waiting for the princess.

00:15:43.166 --> 00:15:46.259
She must come with me to the palace.

00:15:46.319 --> 00:15:51.672
A few moments later, the princess was on the horse behind the Indian.

00:15:51.732 --> 00:15:56.013
They flew up into the air and in the direction of the palace.

00:15:56.073 --> 00:15:59.774
The prince and the king looked up and saw them.

00:15:59.834 --> 00:16:02.415
But the horse didn't land there.

00:16:02.475 --> 00:16:05.916
It flew over the palace and disappeared.

00:16:05.976 --> 00:16:08.427
The prince was afraid.

00:16:08.487 --> 00:16:15.259
The princess is in danger and must go and look for her immediately, he said to his father.

00:16:15.319 --> 00:16:19.528
The horse took the Indian and the princess to India.

00:16:19.588 --> 00:16:24.238
It landed in a forest near the Sultan of Kashmir's palace.

00:16:24.298 --> 00:16:27.712
The princess started shouting for help.

00:16:27.772 --> 00:16:32.234
The Sultan was hunting in the forest that day and he heard her.

00:16:32.294 --> 00:16:34.796
Perhaps that girl is in danger.

00:16:34.856 --> 00:16:38.298
He thought, I must go and save her.

00:16:38.358 --> 00:16:43.262
When he saw the Indian, he pulled out his sword and killed him.

00:16:43.322 --> 00:16:48.464
Then he put the princess on his horse and they rode back to his palace.

00:16:48.524 --> 00:16:53.666
Early the next morning, the princess heard a lot of noise outside her room.

00:16:53.726 --> 00:16:55.358
What's that noise?

00:16:55.418 --> 00:16:56.810
She asked a maid.

00:16:56.870 --> 00:16:59.842
The servants are preparing for your wedding.

00:16:59.902 --> 00:17:02.264
Tomorrow you will marry the Sultan.

00:17:02.324 --> 00:17:03.586
She said.

00:17:03.646 --> 00:17:06.688
The princess was horrified.

00:17:06.748 --> 00:17:08.519
I must do something.

00:17:08.580 --> 00:17:09.430
She thought.

00:17:09.490 --> 00:17:11.442
I can't marry the Sultan.

00:17:11.502 --> 00:17:13.103
I don't love him.

00:17:13.164 --> 00:17:17.690
She started shouting and crying and pulling her hair.

00:17:17.749 --> 00:17:19.623
The maid was afraid.

00:17:19.684 --> 00:17:23.397
She went to the Sultan and said, The princess is ill.

00:17:23.456 --> 00:17:25.888
She can't marry you tomorrow.

00:17:25.948 --> 00:17:28.211
Look after her, he said.

00:17:28.271 --> 00:17:31.634
And we'll get married when she's better.

00:17:31.694 --> 00:17:35.658
But weeks and months passed.

00:17:35.718 --> 00:17:40.864
Many doctors came to see the princess, but she didn't get better.

00:17:40.924 --> 00:17:46.818
Then, one day, a young doctor from Persia arrived at the palace gate.

00:17:46.878 --> 00:17:49.220
It was Prince Farus.

00:17:49.279 --> 00:17:52.352
The princess was very happy to see him.

00:17:52.412 --> 00:17:55.133
We must escape, the prince told her.

00:17:55.193 --> 00:18:01.357
And I have a plan, but first he must stop crying and smile at the Sultan.

00:18:01.417 --> 00:18:06.110
So the princess stopped crying and smiled at the Sultan.

00:18:06.170 --> 00:18:08.168
He was very happy.

00:18:08.228 --> 00:18:12.689
You are a very good doctor," he said to Prince Ferus.

00:18:12.749 --> 00:18:15.170
The Princess is well now.

00:18:15.230 --> 00:18:16.752
You can go home.

00:18:16.812 --> 00:18:20.054
She isn't completely well, the Prince said.

00:18:20.114 --> 00:18:23.296
The enchanted horse put a magic spell on her.

00:18:23.356 --> 00:18:29.080
Bring the horse and the Princess to the square this afternoon, and I'll take away the spell.

00:18:29.140 --> 00:18:33.444
Tell all the people in the town to come and watch.

00:18:33.504 --> 00:18:39.289
At four o'clock that afternoon, the city square was full of people.

00:18:39.350 --> 00:18:42.572
The sultan and the princess were there too.

00:18:42.632 --> 00:18:48.476
When the guards brought the horse, Prince Faroo's made four fires around it.

00:18:48.537 --> 00:18:53.900
He said some strange words and threw some powder into the fires.

00:18:53.960 --> 00:18:56.944
Suddenly, there was a lot of smoke.

00:18:57.004 --> 00:18:59.682
It was impossible to see anything.

00:18:59.742 --> 00:19:08.131
At that moment, Prince Farus and the Princess jumped on the horse's back and the horse flew up into the air.

00:19:08.191 --> 00:19:12.782
Soon they arrived at the King's Palace in Shiraz.

00:19:12.842 --> 00:19:17.654
The King and his people were very happy to see them.

00:19:17.714 --> 00:19:27.230
The next day the Prince and the Princess got married and they lived happily for the rest of their lives.

00:19:27.290 --> 00:19:32.804
Ali Baba and the Forty Thieves.

00:19:32.864 --> 00:19:35.454
Part 1.

00:19:35.514 --> 00:19:39.876
Kazim and Ali Baba were brothers.

00:19:39.936 --> 00:19:42.626
They lived in a city in Persia.

00:19:42.686 --> 00:19:44.547
Kazim was rich.

00:19:44.607 --> 00:19:46.007
He had a shop.

00:19:46.067 --> 00:19:49.588
He bought and sold gold there.

00:19:49.648 --> 00:19:52.329
Ali Baba was poor.

00:19:52.389 --> 00:19:56.602
He collected wood in the forest and sold it in the city.

00:19:56.662 --> 00:20:04.908
One day, while he was collecting wood, Alibaba heard the sound of horses hooves in the distance.

00:20:04.968 --> 00:20:06.850
Who's coming here?

00:20:06.910 --> 00:20:08.180
He asked himself.

00:20:08.240 --> 00:20:11.792
Perhaps they are thieves and want to steal my wood.

00:20:11.852 --> 00:20:13.663
I'll hide in this tree.

00:20:13.723 --> 00:20:18.126
He quickly climbed up the tree and hid in the branches.

00:20:18.186 --> 00:20:20.566
The horseman arrived.

00:20:20.626 --> 00:20:23.583
Alibaba counted 40 men.

00:20:23.643 --> 00:20:28.041
They were big and strong, and they had black beards.

00:20:28.101 --> 00:20:31.453
Each of them had a heavy saddlebag.

00:20:31.514 --> 00:20:32.895
I was right!

00:20:32.955 --> 00:20:34.576
They are thieves!

00:20:34.636 --> 00:20:37.068
thought Alibaba.

00:20:37.128 --> 00:20:40.510
There was a big rock near the tree.

00:20:40.570 --> 00:20:47.446
The captain of the band of thieves went up to it and said, Open Sesame!

00:20:47.506 --> 00:20:51.403
Immediately, a large door opened.

00:20:51.463 --> 00:20:56.871
They all went inside and the door in the rock closed behind them.

00:20:56.931 --> 00:21:01.634
The captain and his men stayed in the cave for a long time.

00:21:01.694 --> 00:21:04.867
Ali Baba began to get tired.

00:21:04.928 --> 00:21:09.170
Suddenly the door opened and they came out.

00:21:09.230 --> 00:21:12.294
Their saddlebags were empty now.

00:21:12.354 --> 00:21:16.126
The captain said, Shut Sesame!

00:21:16.186 --> 00:21:20.006
And the door closed and disappeared.

00:21:20.066 --> 00:21:24.256
Then they got on their horses and rode away.

00:21:24.316 --> 00:21:27.910
Alibaba climbed down the tree.

00:21:27.970 --> 00:21:30.512
I'll try those magic words.

00:21:30.572 --> 00:21:33.946
Perhaps there is treasure in the cave, he thought.

00:21:34.007 --> 00:21:35.878
Open sesame!

00:21:35.938 --> 00:21:39.614
He said, and the door in the rock opened.

00:21:39.674 --> 00:21:44.290
It wasn't very dark inside the cave, so he could see well.

00:21:44.350 --> 00:21:50.946
There were bags of precious tunes, rubies, sapphires and emeralds.

00:21:51.006 --> 00:21:55.289
There were beautiful carpets and silk cloth.

00:21:55.349 --> 00:22:00.213
There were chests full of gold and silver coins.

00:22:00.273 --> 00:22:07.532
Alibaba went back to his donkeys, took his bags, and went inside the cave.

00:22:07.592 --> 00:22:12.018
He filled his bags as quickly as he could with coins.

00:22:12.078 --> 00:22:14.820
Then he hid them under some wood on his donkeys.

00:22:14.840 --> 00:22:20.635
�Shut, sesame!� he said, and the door closed.

00:22:20.696 --> 00:22:27.952
When he arrived home and showed his wife the gold coins, her eyes became as big as dinner plates.

00:22:28.012 --> 00:22:30.196
She started counting them.

00:22:30.256 --> 00:22:33.140
Stupid woman, said Ali Baba.

00:22:33.200 --> 00:22:35.952
Go and get the scales from your sister-in-law.

00:22:36.012 --> 00:22:37.403
We must weigh them.

00:22:37.463 --> 00:22:40.145
There are too many to count.

00:22:40.205 --> 00:22:46.220
Ali Baba's wife went to Khazim's house and asked for the scales.

00:22:46.280 --> 00:22:48.812
Her sister-in-law was surprised.

00:22:48.872 --> 00:22:51.284
Ali Baba is a poor man.

00:22:51.344 --> 00:22:52.284
She thought.

00:22:52.345 --> 00:22:54.458
What does he want to weigh?

00:22:54.518 --> 00:23:02.677
Before giving the scales to Alibaba's wife, she took the cup and put some wax on the bottom of it.

00:23:02.737 --> 00:23:10.423
When Alibaba's wife brought the scales back the next day, her sister-in-law looked at the cup carefully.

00:23:10.484 --> 00:23:14.167
There was a gold coin sticking to the wax.

00:23:14.227 --> 00:23:22.296
That evening, she said to her husband, You think you are rich, but Alibaba has more gold than you.

00:23:22.356 --> 00:23:24.218
He doesn't count his money.

00:23:24.278 --> 00:23:25.820
He weighs it.

00:23:25.880 --> 00:23:29.174
Kazim didn't sleep that night.

00:23:29.234 --> 00:23:32.120
He thought about his brother's gold.

00:23:32.180 --> 00:23:37.963
The next morning, he went to Alibaba's house and showed him the gold coin.

00:23:38.023 --> 00:23:44.744
He said, Brother, you say you are poor, but I know that you weigh your gold.

00:23:44.804 --> 00:23:48.145
My wife found this coin in the cup of the scales.

00:23:48.205 --> 00:23:50.305
Where did you get it?

00:23:50.365 --> 00:23:56.896
Alibaba was an honest man, so he told Kazim about the cave in the forest.

00:23:56.956 --> 00:24:02.386
When he heard about the treasure, Kazim wanted some of the gold too.

00:24:02.446 --> 00:24:12.978
Without saying anything to his wife, or Alibaba, he took ten donkeys, each with two bags, and went to the forest.

00:24:13.038 --> 00:24:19.051
He found the rock, and said the magic words, Open Sesame!

00:24:19.111 --> 00:24:21.152
The door opened.

00:24:21.212 --> 00:24:28.114
He went inside the cave, and immediately started filling his bags with coins and jewels.

00:24:28.174 --> 00:24:33.670
While he was filling the last bag, he heard the sound of horses hooves outside.

00:24:33.730 --> 00:24:35.481
The thieves, he thought.

00:24:35.542 --> 00:24:36.892
What shall I do?

00:24:36.952 --> 00:24:38.134
They'll kill me.

00:24:38.194 --> 00:24:39.565
Where can I hide?

00:24:39.625 --> 00:24:46.162
He looked around the cave, but at that moment the door opened and the captain came in.

00:24:46.222 --> 00:24:52.607
Kazim tried to escape, but the captain caught him and killed him with his sword.

00:24:52.667 --> 00:24:55.708
Perhaps other people know about the cave.

00:24:55.769 --> 00:25:01.032
We'll leave his body here as a warning to them," said the captain.

00:25:01.092 --> 00:25:07.875
He cut Kasim's body into four pieces and put them around the door of the cave.

00:25:07.936 --> 00:25:17.802
Then, after putting the gold and silver back in the chests, the captain and the thieves left.

00:25:17.862 --> 00:25:25.954
Part 2 Kasim's wife was worried about her husband.

00:25:26.014 --> 00:25:27.996
He was late for dinner.

00:25:28.056 --> 00:25:30.397
She went to see Alibaba.

00:25:30.457 --> 00:25:31.818
Brother-in-law?

00:25:31.878 --> 00:25:32.558
She said.

00:25:32.618 --> 00:25:34.529
I'm worried about Kasim.

00:25:34.589 --> 00:25:36.050
He's very late.

00:25:36.110 --> 00:25:37.851
Please go and find him.

00:25:37.911 --> 00:25:40.842
Tell him that I'm waiting to serve dinner.

00:25:40.903 --> 00:25:44.515
Alibaba knew that his brother liked gold.

00:25:44.575 --> 00:25:45.756
He thought...

00:25:45.816 --> 00:25:48.447
Perhaps Kasim is in the cave.

00:25:48.507 --> 00:25:50.812
I'll go there first.

00:25:50.873 --> 00:25:58.721
When he opened the door of the cave and saw the pieces of his brother's body around the door, he was afraid.

00:25:58.782 --> 00:26:01.123
The thieves will kill me next.

00:26:01.183 --> 00:26:01.953
He thought.

00:26:02.014 --> 00:26:04.215
I must get out of here quickly.

00:26:04.275 --> 00:26:09.828
Before he left, he filmed his bags with gold and put them on his donkeys.

00:26:09.888 --> 00:26:16.442
Then he put Kasim's body in another bag and rode back to his sister-in-law's house.

00:26:16.502 --> 00:26:20.390
One of Kasim's slaves opened the door.

00:26:20.450 --> 00:26:22.986
Her name was Mortjana.

00:26:23.047 --> 00:26:29.502
Alibaba gave her the bag with Kazim's body and some instructions about the funeral.

00:26:29.562 --> 00:26:32.594
Then he went to see his sister-in-law.

00:26:32.654 --> 00:26:36.366
She cried when she heard that her husband was dead.

00:26:36.426 --> 00:26:37.807
Sister-in-law?

00:26:37.867 --> 00:26:38.748
He said.

00:26:38.808 --> 00:26:40.369
We're in danger.

00:26:40.429 --> 00:26:43.101
Nobody must know how Kazim died.

00:26:43.161 --> 00:26:45.068
It must be a secret.

00:26:45.128 --> 00:26:48.677
Then he told her about the treasure and the thieves.

00:26:48.737 --> 00:26:51.108
Don't worry, he said.

00:26:51.168 --> 00:26:52.819
I'm rich now.

00:26:52.879 --> 00:26:55.470
I'll marry you and look after you.

00:26:55.530 --> 00:26:58.842
My wife and I will come and live in this house.

00:26:58.902 --> 00:27:04.116
When Kasim's wife heard this, she stopped crying.

00:27:04.176 --> 00:27:07.288
Morjana was a clever girl.

00:27:07.348 --> 00:27:13.642
She understood Alibaba's instructions about Kasim's funeral, and she knew what to do.

00:27:13.702 --> 00:27:19.135
She went to see Baba Mustafa, the shoemaker, in the market.

00:27:19.195 --> 00:27:25.948
She gave him a gold coin and said, I have a special job for you Baba Mustafa.

00:27:26.008 --> 00:27:29.829
Cover your eyes with this cloth and come with me.

00:27:29.889 --> 00:27:35.421
He was a poor man, so he took the coin and covered his eyes.

00:27:35.481 --> 00:27:40.900
Morjana took him through the streets of Baghdad to Qasim's house.

00:27:40.960 --> 00:27:45.128
When he took off the cloth, he was in a dark room.

00:27:45.188 --> 00:27:47.950
So those pieces together again?

00:27:48.010 --> 00:27:53.422
She said to him, and pointed to the four pieces of Kazim's body on a table.

00:27:53.482 --> 00:27:56.294
Then make a bag for the body.

00:27:56.354 --> 00:27:59.676
Mustafa worked all day.

00:27:59.736 --> 00:28:09.622
When the body was in the bag, Morjana gave Mustafa another gold coin, covered his eyes, and took him back to his shop.

00:28:09.683 --> 00:28:16.058
Three days after Cassim's funeral, Alibaba moved into his house.

00:28:16.118 --> 00:28:20.911
In the meantime, the thieves returned to the cave.

00:28:20.971 --> 00:28:23.182
Where's the body of that man?

00:28:23.242 --> 00:28:24.913
Where's our gold?

00:28:24.973 --> 00:28:27.254
They asked angrily.

00:28:27.315 --> 00:28:31.336
The captain said, someone knows the magic words.

00:28:31.396 --> 00:28:36.245
We must find him and kill him before he steals the rest of our treasure.

00:28:36.305 --> 00:28:42.252
He told his best man to dress himself as a merchant and go to the city.

00:28:42.312 --> 00:28:47.374
Come back when you find the man who knows the magic words, he said.

00:28:47.434 --> 00:28:53.936
It was early morning and still dark when the thief arrived in the market square.

00:28:53.996 --> 00:28:56.386
Only Mustafa was awake.

00:28:56.446 --> 00:28:59.822
He was sewing shoes outside his shop.

00:28:59.882 --> 00:29:02.289
How can you see to sow?"

00:29:02.349 --> 00:29:03.460
asked the thief.

00:29:03.520 --> 00:29:04.911
It's dark.

00:29:04.971 --> 00:29:09.204
I am old, but my eyes are still good.

00:29:09.264 --> 00:29:10.855
replied Mustafa.

00:29:10.915 --> 00:29:17.340
Yesterday I sowed four pieces of a body together in a dark room.

00:29:17.400 --> 00:29:23.864
Take me to that house, and I'll give you these gold coins, said the thief.

00:29:23.924 --> 00:29:27.026
Mustafa put the coins in his pocket.

00:29:27.086 --> 00:29:29.520
Follow me, he said.

00:29:29.580 --> 00:29:34.936
He had a good memory, so it wasn't difficult for him to remember the way.

00:29:34.996 --> 00:29:43.750
When they arrived at Alibaba's house, the thief took out a piece of white chalk and put a cross on the door.

00:29:43.810 --> 00:29:48.964
Then he thanked Mustafa and rode back to the forest.

00:29:49.024 --> 00:29:52.746
Morjana returned home from the market.

00:29:52.806 --> 00:29:56.018
She was surprised to see the cross on the door.

00:29:56.078 --> 00:29:59.144
Perhaps someone wants to hurt my master.

00:29:59.204 --> 00:30:04.954
She thought, and she put a white cross on all the other doors in the street.

00:30:05.014 --> 00:30:11.420
When the captain arrived and saw that there were white crosses on all the doors, he was angry.

00:30:11.480 --> 00:30:16.404
He rode back to the forest and killed his best man.

00:30:16.464 --> 00:30:21.718
The next day, he sent his second best man to Mustafa.

00:30:21.779 --> 00:30:26.100
This time, the thief put a red cross on the door.

00:30:26.160 --> 00:30:31.880
Morgana saw the cross and put red crosses on all the other doors.

00:30:31.940 --> 00:30:38.803
When the captain arrived and saw that there were red crosses on all the doors, he was angrier than before.

00:30:38.863 --> 00:30:43.665
He rode back to the forest and killed his second best man.

00:30:43.725 --> 00:30:49.128
Tomorrow, I will go and find this man's house, he said.

00:30:49.188 --> 00:30:54.016
When he returned from the city, he called his men together.

00:30:54.076 --> 00:31:02.766
We must kill this man and take back our golden jewels," he said, and I have a plan.

00:31:02.826 --> 00:31:13.090
Part 3 The captain told his men to bring him 38 big oil jars.

00:31:13.150 --> 00:31:19.323
He filled one of the jars with oil and told his men to climb into the others.

00:31:19.383 --> 00:31:22.544
Then he put the jars on donkeys.

00:31:22.604 --> 00:31:28.168
He dressed himself as a merchant and rode to Alibaba's house.

00:31:28.228 --> 00:31:31.170
Mojana opened the door.

00:31:31.231 --> 00:31:34.363
I'm an oil merchant, he said.

00:31:34.423 --> 00:31:38.566
All the hotels in the city are full and it's late.

00:31:38.626 --> 00:31:42.510
Can the master of the house give me a bed for the night?

00:31:42.570 --> 00:31:45.693
Alibaba was happy to help the merchant.

00:31:45.754 --> 00:31:48.506
Tell him to leave his jars downstairs.

00:31:48.566 --> 00:31:50.831
He said to Mojana.

00:31:50.891 --> 00:31:56.896
After dinner, the captain went downstairs and whispered to his men in the jars.

00:31:56.956 --> 00:32:00.637
When I say, it's time.

00:32:00.698 --> 00:32:04.188
Break the jars and come upstairs.

00:32:04.248 --> 00:32:06.709
Then he went to bed.

00:32:06.769 --> 00:32:09.290
Morejana was in the kitchen.

00:32:09.350 --> 00:32:14.011
She wanted to make some soup, but she didn't have any oil.

00:32:14.071 --> 00:32:17.132
The merchant's jars are full of oil.

00:32:17.192 --> 00:32:18.162
She thought.

00:32:18.222 --> 00:32:20.524
I'll take some from one of them.

00:32:20.584 --> 00:32:24.496
She took her pan and went downstairs.

00:32:24.556 --> 00:32:32.514
While she was closing the door, a voice from inside one of the jars said, is it time yet?

00:32:32.574 --> 00:32:34.826
She was very surprised.

00:32:34.886 --> 00:32:38.948
She answered, no, it isn't time yet.

00:32:39.008 --> 00:32:41.420
She went to another jar.

00:32:41.480 --> 00:32:44.976
A voice said, is it time yet?

00:32:45.036 --> 00:32:47.888
She gave the same answer as before.

00:32:47.948 --> 00:32:51.929
She went to the other jars, one by one.

00:32:51.989 --> 00:32:58.000
She heard the same question from inside each one, and she gave the same answer.

00:32:58.060 --> 00:33:00.771
Only one jar didn't speak.

00:33:00.831 --> 00:33:02.521
She opened it.

00:33:02.581 --> 00:33:05.081
It was full of oil.

00:33:05.141 --> 00:33:08.712
She filled her pan and went back upstairs.

00:33:08.772 --> 00:33:11.972
The merchant wants to kill my master.

00:33:12.032 --> 00:33:15.256
She thought, I must do something.

00:33:15.316 --> 00:33:19.440
She heated the oil on the fire until it was very hot.

00:33:19.500 --> 00:33:25.912
Then she went downstairs and poured some of the boiling oil into each of the jars.

00:33:25.972 --> 00:33:29.794
Now we are all safe and I can sleep in peace.

00:33:29.854 --> 00:33:32.596
Morjana said to herself.

00:33:32.656 --> 00:33:37.078
At midnight, the captain came downstairs.

00:33:37.138 --> 00:33:38.838
It's time!

00:33:38.898 --> 00:33:40.549
He whispered.

00:33:40.610 --> 00:33:42.812
Nothing happened.

00:33:42.873 --> 00:33:46.428
He opened one of the jars and looked inside.

00:33:46.488 --> 00:33:48.759
He was horrified.

00:33:48.819 --> 00:33:51.331
He looked inside the other jars.

00:33:51.391 --> 00:33:55.554
All his men were dead, boiled in oil.

00:33:55.614 --> 00:33:58.346
Ali Baba is a dangerous man.

00:33:58.406 --> 00:34:02.700
He thought, and he ran back to the forest.

00:34:02.760 --> 00:34:08.344
Ali Baba saw the jars the next day and asked more Jana.

00:34:08.404 --> 00:34:11.124
Why are the merchants jars still here?

00:34:11.184 --> 00:34:14.624
Morjana showed him the bodies in the jars.

00:34:14.684 --> 00:34:16.325
Well done!

00:34:16.385 --> 00:34:18.777
You are a very clever girl.

00:34:18.837 --> 00:34:21.048
Ali Baba said.

00:34:21.109 --> 00:34:24.090
Many months passed.

00:34:24.151 --> 00:34:32.416
The captain changed his name to Kawaja Hussein and bought a shop in the market square.

00:34:32.476 --> 00:34:36.068
He sold the cloth and carpets from the cave.

00:34:36.129 --> 00:34:39.440
He became friends with the other shopkeepers.

00:34:39.500 --> 00:34:42.096
One of them was a young man.

00:34:42.156 --> 00:34:46.301
One day, Alibaba visited the young man's shop.

00:34:46.361 --> 00:34:48.442
The captain saw him.

00:34:48.502 --> 00:34:54.494
Later, he asked his young friend, who was that man in your shop today?

00:34:54.554 --> 00:34:57.325
That was my father, Alibaba.

00:34:57.385 --> 00:34:59.046
The boy replied.

00:34:59.106 --> 00:35:01.346
The captain was surprised.

00:35:01.406 --> 00:35:04.167
That's interesting, he thought.

00:35:04.227 --> 00:35:07.773
He still wanted to kill Alibaba.

00:35:07.833 --> 00:35:18.672
Some weeks after that, Alibaba's son went to his father and said, Father, I would like to invite my friend, Kawaja, who's saying, to dinner tomorrow.

00:35:18.732 --> 00:35:21.933
Of course, replied Alibaba.

00:35:21.993 --> 00:35:25.724
I'll ask Morgana to make something special to eat.

00:35:25.784 --> 00:35:30.776
The next evening, the captain arrived at Alibaba's house.

00:35:30.837 --> 00:35:37.871
When Morgana saw him, she said to herself, But this is the merchant who wanted to kill my master.

00:35:37.932 --> 00:35:39.612
He has another plot.

00:35:39.672 --> 00:35:42.114
I must do something."

00:35:42.174 --> 00:35:47.886
She served dinner, and then she put on a very beautiful dress.

00:35:47.946 --> 00:35:56.701
She went to the cook, and said, Tonight I'm going to dance for our master's guest, and you're going to play the tambourine for me.

00:35:56.761 --> 00:35:59.552
Come, let's go to them now.

00:35:59.612 --> 00:36:03.279
Morgana danced some beautiful dancers.

00:36:03.339 --> 00:36:06.136
The last one was very exciting.

00:36:06.196 --> 00:36:09.028
She had a dagger in her hand.

00:36:09.088 --> 00:36:15.672
After this dance, Morjana took the tambourine from the cook and went to the men.

00:36:15.732 --> 00:36:20.026
Both Alibaba and his son put a gold coin in it.

00:36:20.086 --> 00:36:22.527
Then she went to the captain.

00:36:22.588 --> 00:36:26.150
He put his hand in his pocket to take out some money.

00:36:26.210 --> 00:36:33.515
But just at that moment, Morjana took her dagger and plunged it into his heart.

00:36:33.575 --> 00:36:35.686
He fell to the floor.

00:36:35.746 --> 00:36:37.256
Dead.

00:36:37.317 --> 00:36:39.677
Alibaba was shocked.

00:36:39.737 --> 00:36:42.428
Morgana, why did you do that?

00:36:42.488 --> 00:36:43.329
He said.

00:36:43.389 --> 00:36:47.680
He was the captain of the band of thieves and he wanted to kill you.

00:36:47.740 --> 00:36:49.321
She replied.

00:36:49.381 --> 00:36:55.324
She lifted the man's jacket and showed Alibaba the knife in his belt.

00:36:55.384 --> 00:36:58.555
You are a very clever woman Morgana.

00:36:58.615 --> 00:37:00.063
He said.

00:37:00.124 --> 00:37:07.774
Then he looked at his son and said to him, Son, you must marry Mojana.

00:37:07.834 --> 00:37:12.896
She is the cleverest woman in Persia.

00:37:12.956 --> 00:37:20.829
The second voyage of Sinbad the Sailor, part one.

00:37:20.889 --> 00:37:26.351
There was once a sailor from Baghdad called Sinbad.

00:37:26.411 --> 00:37:30.086
He made seven long voyages in his life.

00:37:30.146 --> 00:37:33.290
They were all full of adventures.

00:37:33.350 --> 00:37:39.202
He met many strange people and saw many strange things.

00:37:39.262 --> 00:37:46.424
When he was old, he liked telling people about his adventures and they liked listening.

00:37:46.484 --> 00:37:50.876
This is the story of his second voyage.

00:37:50.936 --> 00:37:58.207
When I returned home from my first voyage, I lived a comfortable life in the city for some years.

00:37:58.267 --> 00:38:00.987
Then I began to get bored.

00:38:01.048 --> 00:38:03.690
I dreamt of sailing the seas again.

00:38:03.750 --> 00:38:06.232
I wanted new adventures.

00:38:06.292 --> 00:38:11.598
One morning I packed my chest and travelled to the port of Basra.

00:38:11.658 --> 00:38:16.812
There was a good strong ship in the harbour and it was ready to sail.

00:38:16.872 --> 00:38:18.524
I got on it.

00:38:18.584 --> 00:38:23.462
We travelled from port to port and from island to island.

00:38:23.522 --> 00:38:30.867
The other passengers on the ship were merchants and when we stopped they bought and sold things.

00:38:30.927 --> 00:38:34.238
Soon I began to do the same.

00:38:34.298 --> 00:38:39.630
Weeks and months passed pleasantly but without adventure.

00:38:39.690 --> 00:38:46.462
Then one day the wind took our ship to a strange and beautiful island.

00:38:46.522 --> 00:38:54.016
There were trees with delicious fruit, flowers of many colours and streams of sweet water.

00:38:54.076 --> 00:39:00.188
The air was full of the songs of birds, but there weren't any people.

00:39:00.248 --> 00:39:04.690
The other passengers started to explore the island.

00:39:04.750 --> 00:39:08.930
I was tired, so I sat under a tree.

00:39:08.990 --> 00:39:16.872
I ate some of the delicious fruit from the trees and drank some of the sweet water from the streams.

00:39:16.932 --> 00:39:19.913
Then I fell asleep.

00:39:19.973 --> 00:39:23.475
When I woke up, I looked around.

00:39:23.535 --> 00:39:26.058
I was alone on the island.

00:39:26.118 --> 00:39:30.380
I looked out to sea and saw my ship on the horizon.

00:39:30.440 --> 00:39:33.022
I began to feel afraid.

00:39:33.082 --> 00:39:35.273
Oh, poor me!

00:39:35.333 --> 00:39:38.936
I said, what shall I do now?

00:39:38.996 --> 00:39:42.788
I walked around the island for an hour or more.

00:39:42.848 --> 00:39:46.230
Then I climbed a tall tree.

00:39:46.290 --> 00:39:51.931
I can get a better view of the island from the top of a tree, I thought.

00:39:51.992 --> 00:40:00.606
I looked left and right, but I saw only trees, flowers, birds, the sea and the sky.

00:40:00.667 --> 00:40:03.960
Then I looked more carefully.

00:40:04.020 --> 00:40:08.543
There was a big white object in the distance.

00:40:08.603 --> 00:40:12.026
I decided to go and have a look at it.

00:40:12.086 --> 00:40:16.530
When I got nearer, I saw that it was a dome.

00:40:16.590 --> 00:40:19.946
I touched it and walked round it.

00:40:20.006 --> 00:40:27.594
It was very smooth and very big, but there were no doors or windows in it.

00:40:27.654 --> 00:40:31.145
Suddenly, it became dark.

00:40:31.205 --> 00:40:34.767
I looked up and saw an enormous bird above me.

00:40:34.827 --> 00:40:36.967
It covered the sun.

00:40:37.028 --> 00:40:38.668
A rock!

00:40:38.728 --> 00:40:44.332
I said to myself, and this white dome is her egg.

00:40:44.392 --> 00:40:48.503
I remembered a traveler's story about these birds.

00:40:48.563 --> 00:40:53.174
It said that rocks caught elephants for their babies to eat.

00:40:53.234 --> 00:41:00.068
Just at that moment the bird landed on top of her egg and soon she was asleep.

00:41:00.128 --> 00:41:08.060
I quickly took off my turban and tied one end of it to the rocks foot and the other around my waist.

00:41:08.120 --> 00:41:15.323
Perhaps this bird will take me to a land where there are cities and people, I thought.

00:41:15.383 --> 00:41:18.258
I waited all night.

00:41:18.318 --> 00:41:25.276
In the morning the rock woke up and flew away and she took me with her.

00:41:25.337 --> 00:41:28.038
She didn't take me very far.

00:41:28.098 --> 00:41:31.030
We landed on the side of a mountain.

00:41:31.091 --> 00:41:36.705
I quickly untied my turban and hid behind a rock.

00:41:36.765 --> 00:41:43.120
The rock picked up a huge snake in its talons and flew away.

00:41:43.180 --> 00:41:45.212
I looked around me.

00:41:45.272 --> 00:41:47.800
I saw a lot more snakes.

00:41:47.860 --> 00:41:50.820
They were sleeping among the rocks.

00:41:50.880 --> 00:41:55.764
This is a terrible place, I thought.

00:41:55.824 --> 00:42:04.402
There was fruit to eat and water to drink on the island, but there are only snakes here.

00:42:04.462 --> 00:42:15.943
Listening activity The island of Sri Lanka is in the Indian Ocean, southeast of India.

00:42:16.003 --> 00:42:23.626
It is shaped like a big pair, with the small part in the north and the large part in the south.

00:42:23.687 --> 00:42:33.679
The greatest length is 440 kilometres, and the greatest width is 220 kilometres.

00:42:33.740 --> 00:42:38.832
The largest city, Colombo, is on the west coast.

00:42:38.892 --> 00:42:48.856
The port town of Trinko Mali is on the northeast coast, It has one of the best natural harbors in the world.

00:42:48.916 --> 00:42:51.867
Gal is another port town.

00:42:51.927 --> 00:42:55.028
It is on the southwest coast.

00:42:55.088 --> 00:43:01.070
In the south-central part of the island, there are many high mountains.

00:43:01.130 --> 00:43:06.042
The highest mountain is Mount Peduro Talagala.

00:43:06.102 --> 00:43:09.354
It is 2524 metres high.

00:43:09.414 --> 00:43:15.256
In the north, the land is flat and dry.

00:43:15.316 --> 00:43:22.330
There are many rivers and streams in Sri Lanka, especially in the south central region.

00:43:22.390 --> 00:43:26.742
The longest river is the Mahaweli Ganga.

00:43:26.803 --> 00:43:30.645
It is 335 km long.

00:43:30.705 --> 00:43:41.522
It starts in the mountains, in the south central region, and empties into the Indian Ocean south of Trinkomali.

00:43:41.582 --> 00:43:49.398
Part 2 I walked down into the valley.

00:43:49.458 --> 00:43:54.910
There weren't any trees or flowers, only sand and rocks.

00:43:54.971 --> 00:44:00.143
The small stones under my feet sparkled in the sunshine.

00:44:00.203 --> 00:44:03.054
I looked at them more carefully.

00:44:03.114 --> 00:44:05.505
They weren't stones.

00:44:05.566 --> 00:44:07.566
They were diamonds.

00:44:07.627 --> 00:44:10.949
Then I knew where I was.

00:44:11.009 --> 00:44:16.082
This is the valley of diamonds," I said to myself.

00:44:16.142 --> 00:44:19.084
Nobody escapes from here.

00:44:19.144 --> 00:44:22.725
I began to feel very afraid.

00:44:22.785 --> 00:44:24.676
I looked around.

00:44:24.736 --> 00:44:28.197
The snakes were still asleep among the rocks.

00:44:28.258 --> 00:44:32.259
Their bodies were as thick as tree trunks.

00:44:32.319 --> 00:44:38.787
They'll wake up when it is dark, I thought, and come out to look for food.

00:44:38.847 --> 00:44:42.463
I must find a safe place to sleep tonight.

00:44:42.523 --> 00:44:45.764
Perhaps there are some caves here."

00:44:45.824 --> 00:44:51.066
It was beginning to get dark, and I could hear the snakes.

00:44:51.126 --> 00:44:54.097
They were waking up.

00:44:54.117 --> 00:44:55.608
I walked faster.

00:44:55.668 --> 00:44:58.109
Soon I found a cave.

00:44:58.169 --> 00:45:03.300
It was big and dark inside, but the floor was dry.

00:45:03.360 --> 00:45:07.378
This is a good place to sleep, I thought.

00:45:07.438 --> 00:45:12.585
I'll put a big rock in the mouth of the cave to keep the snakes out.

00:45:12.645 --> 00:45:16.106
I'll be safe here until the morning.

00:45:16.167 --> 00:45:19.678
I went in and looked around.

00:45:19.738 --> 00:45:25.241
At the back of the cave, I could see two small red lights.

00:45:25.301 --> 00:45:27.642
Two eyes.

00:45:27.702 --> 00:45:30.724
There was a huge snake there.

00:45:30.784 --> 00:45:33.895
She was sitting on her eggs.

00:45:33.955 --> 00:45:36.200
She was looking at me.

00:45:36.260 --> 00:45:38.555
I ran out of the cave.

00:45:38.615 --> 00:45:44.798
It was completely dark in the valley now, and the snakes in the rocks were coming out.

00:45:44.858 --> 00:45:47.519
They made a terrible noise.

00:45:47.579 --> 00:45:50.040
I was very afraid.

00:45:50.100 --> 00:45:53.712
I decided to stay in the cave.

00:45:53.772 --> 00:46:02.640
One snake is better than a hundred, I thought, and she is more interested in her eggs than she is in me.

00:46:02.700 --> 00:46:07.720
So I found a rock and closed the cave.

00:46:07.780 --> 00:46:10.514
I was awake all night.

00:46:10.574 --> 00:46:13.126
I could hear the snakes outside.

00:46:13.187 --> 00:46:15.368
The noise was terrible.

00:46:15.428 --> 00:46:21.344
The snake at the back of the cave sat on her eggs and looked at me.

00:46:21.404 --> 00:46:27.538
When I saw the first light from the sun, I moved the rock and went out.

00:46:27.598 --> 00:46:29.540
It was quiet.

00:46:29.600 --> 00:46:35.714
The snakes were asleep, so I left the cave and started walking down the valley.

00:46:35.774 --> 00:46:41.408
Suddenly something fell out of the sky and landed at my feet.

00:46:41.468 --> 00:46:44.250
It was a big piece of meat.

00:46:44.310 --> 00:46:47.902
Then another piece of meat fell out of the sky.

00:46:47.962 --> 00:46:50.291
I was very surprised.

00:46:50.351 --> 00:46:55.620
but I remembered another traveler's story about the Valley of Diamonds.

00:46:55.680 --> 00:47:07.886
The story said that diamond merchants never came into the valley because it was a very dangerous place, but they had a very clever way of getting the diamonds out.

00:47:07.946 --> 00:47:15.290
They stood on the tops of the mountains and threw big pieces of meat down into the valley.

00:47:15.350 --> 00:47:20.592
The meat was soft, so the precious stones stuck to it.

00:47:20.652 --> 00:47:26.176
At midday rocks and eagles flew down into the valley.

00:47:26.236 --> 00:47:32.220
They picked up the pieces of meat and carried them up to the tops of the mountains.

00:47:32.281 --> 00:47:38.676
When the birds landed, the merchants shouted loudly and made a lot of noise.

00:47:38.736 --> 00:47:42.799
The birds were afraid and flew away.

00:47:42.859 --> 00:47:49.686
Then the merchants took the diamonds out of the meat and put them into chests.

00:47:49.746 --> 00:47:55.039
This was the only way of getting the diamonds out of the valley.

00:47:55.099 --> 00:48:01.572
Later the merchants sold the precious stones in the cities for a lot of money.

00:48:01.632 --> 00:48:04.674
The story gave me an idea.

00:48:04.734 --> 00:48:09.156
I filled my pockets with the biggest diamonds I could find.

00:48:09.216 --> 00:48:14.368
Then I tied myself to a piece of meat with my turban.

00:48:14.428 --> 00:48:17.648
Soon an eagle came down.

00:48:17.708 --> 00:48:24.458
It picked up the piece of meat and me and flew up to the top of a mountain with it.

00:48:24.518 --> 00:48:29.450
As soon as we landed, there was a lot of noise and shouting.

00:48:29.510 --> 00:48:33.040
The bird was afraid and flew away.

00:48:33.100 --> 00:48:36.972
I untied myself quickly and started to run.

00:48:37.032 --> 00:48:37.892
Hey!

00:48:37.952 --> 00:48:38.542
You!

00:48:38.602 --> 00:48:39.642
Stop!

00:48:39.702 --> 00:48:41.363
A man shouted.

00:48:41.423 --> 00:48:43.202
I stopped.

00:48:43.263 --> 00:48:46.113
Don't hurt me, sir," I said.

00:48:46.173 --> 00:48:47.844
I'm an honest man.

00:48:47.904 --> 00:48:50.215
I don't want your diamonds.

00:48:50.275 --> 00:48:54.888
I took three big diamonds out of my pocket.

00:48:54.948 --> 00:48:57.008
Look, I said.

00:48:57.069 --> 00:48:58.229
Take these.

00:48:58.289 --> 00:49:00.260
I picked them up in the valley.

00:49:00.320 --> 00:49:03.102
And I gave him the stones.

00:49:03.162 --> 00:49:07.214
The man was very happy and thanked me.

00:49:07.274 --> 00:49:09.944
He took me to meet his friends.

00:49:10.004 --> 00:49:12.942
They were all diamond merchants.

00:49:13.002 --> 00:49:17.939
They gave me food and drink and listened to my story.

00:49:17.999 --> 00:49:25.342
One of them said, You're the first man to escape from this valley.

00:49:25.402 --> 00:49:28.954
I traveled with them for many weeks.

00:49:29.014 --> 00:49:34.286
We visited many countries and we had many adventures.

00:49:34.346 --> 00:49:39.798
I gave them diamonds and they gave me food and drink.

00:49:39.858 --> 00:49:44.471
In one port there was a ship that was going to Basra.

00:49:44.532 --> 00:49:51.236
I was tired of travelling and I wanted to see my family again, so I got on it.

00:49:51.296 --> 00:49:55.300
From Basra I travelled back to Baghdad.

00:49:55.360 --> 00:49:58.452
I was happy to be home again.

00:49:58.512 --> 00:50:00.934
I was a rich man.

00:50:00.994 --> 00:50:06.898
I gave many presents to my family and money to the poor people of the city.

00:50:06.958 --> 00:50:10.691
I enjoyed my comfortable life at home.

00:50:10.751 --> 00:50:15.294
But after a few years, I started to get bored.

00:50:15.354 --> 00:50:22.708
I wanted to travel the seas again and have new adventures.

00:50:22.768 --> 00:50:38.504
The Story of the Young King of the Black Islands Part 1 When King Mahmoud of the Black Islands died, his young son became king.

00:50:38.564 --> 00:50:42.804
A few weeks later, he married his cousin.

00:50:42.864 --> 00:50:49.170
The young king loved his wife very much, and he thought that she loved him.

00:50:49.230 --> 00:50:51.002
He was happy.

00:50:51.062 --> 00:50:55.767
But she was not a good wife, and she didn't love him.

00:50:55.827 --> 00:50:59.661
She also had magic powers.

00:50:59.721 --> 00:51:04.514
The king and the queen lived happily for five years.

00:51:04.574 --> 00:51:11.134
Then one afternoon, the young king heard a conversation between two of his wife's maids.

00:51:11.194 --> 00:51:14.456
They didn't know that he was listening to them.

00:51:14.516 --> 00:51:18.486
It's sad that the queen doesn't love the king, isn't it?

00:51:18.546 --> 00:51:19.847
One of them said.

00:51:19.907 --> 00:51:21.487
Yes, it is.

00:51:21.547 --> 00:51:23.118
The other maid replied.

00:51:23.178 --> 00:51:24.998
She's a bad woman.

00:51:25.058 --> 00:51:28.669
Every night she puts a sleep in potion in his wine.

00:51:28.729 --> 00:51:33.656
Then when he is asleep, she goes out to meet her lover in the forest.

00:51:33.716 --> 00:51:36.654
The young king was horrified.

00:51:36.714 --> 00:51:40.636
He decided to watch his wife carefully.

00:51:40.696 --> 00:51:49.318
That night, he didn't drink his wine, so he wasn't asleep when the queen got out of bed and left the palace.

00:51:49.378 --> 00:51:52.019
He followed her to the forest.

00:51:52.079 --> 00:51:56.620
Her lover was there, and they kissed passionately.

00:51:56.680 --> 00:52:01.228
When the young king saw them together, he was very angry.

00:52:01.288 --> 00:52:05.096
took out his sword and hit the man on the neck.

00:52:05.156 --> 00:52:07.608
The man fell to the ground.

00:52:07.668 --> 00:52:14.313
Then the young king ran back to the palace before the queen had time to see his face.

00:52:14.373 --> 00:52:18.776
The next morning, the queen came to his room.

00:52:18.836 --> 00:52:24.594
She was wearing black clothes, and she was crying.

00:52:24.654 --> 00:52:33.602
I'm mourning my family, my father, my mother, and my two brothers are all dead."

00:52:33.662 --> 00:52:36.404
The young king said nothing.

00:52:36.464 --> 00:52:39.815
He knew that it was not true.

00:52:39.876 --> 00:52:43.086
The queen mourned for a year.

00:52:43.146 --> 00:52:51.881
At the end of this time, she built a black dome in the palace garden and filmed it with precious carpets and paintings.

00:52:51.941 --> 00:52:54.851
Then she took her lover's body there.

00:52:54.911 --> 00:52:59.424
He wasn't dead, but he couldn't move or speak.

00:52:59.484 --> 00:53:05.698
She put him on a sofa in a dark room and built a beautiful fountain for him there.

00:53:05.758 --> 00:53:11.234
She went to see him every day and gave him soup and wine to drink.

00:53:11.294 --> 00:53:14.296
She cried all the time.

00:53:14.356 --> 00:53:17.436
Three years passed.

00:53:17.496 --> 00:53:22.414
One day, the young king went to the dome to speak to his wife.

00:53:22.475 --> 00:53:24.936
She was crying as usual.

00:53:24.996 --> 00:53:27.296
He was very angry.

00:53:27.356 --> 00:53:29.877
I'm tired of your tears.

00:53:29.937 --> 00:53:32.708
He shouted, and he took out his sword.

00:53:32.768 --> 00:53:34.829
You're a bad woman.

00:53:34.889 --> 00:53:37.530
I know that you keep your lover here.

00:53:37.590 --> 00:53:38.960
Yes, I do.

00:53:39.020 --> 00:53:40.361
The queen replied.

00:53:40.421 --> 00:53:43.164
I love him, and I hate you.

00:53:43.224 --> 00:53:50.292
The king lifted his sword to kill her, but the queen put a magic spell on him before he could hit her.

00:53:50.352 --> 00:53:54.976
She turned his legs into a block of black marble.

00:53:55.036 --> 00:53:57.367
He couldn't move.

00:53:57.427 --> 00:54:10.936
Then she turned the four islands into four mountains, the city into a lake, and the people in the city, into fish.

00:54:10.996 --> 00:54:19.140
After that, the Queen visited the black dome every day.

00:54:19.200 --> 00:54:25.394
First she went to her husband, and beat him one hundred times with a whip.

00:54:25.455 --> 00:54:30.790
He cried and shouted loudly, but her heart was hard.

00:54:30.850 --> 00:54:33.552
Then she went to her lover.

00:54:33.612 --> 00:54:39.356
After giving him some soup and wine she said, How are you today, my love?

00:54:39.416 --> 00:54:40.958
Speak to me.

00:54:41.018 --> 00:54:45.038
But he never moved, and he never spoke.

00:54:45.098 --> 00:54:51.340
Some years later, a king from a distant country travelled to the Black Islands.

00:54:51.400 --> 00:54:56.024
He went in the Black Dome and found the young king.

00:54:56.084 --> 00:55:00.936
When he heard his story, he felt very sorry for him.

00:55:00.996 --> 00:55:03.168
He promised to help him.

00:55:03.228 --> 00:55:06.470
I have a plan, he said.

00:55:06.530 --> 00:55:11.736
The next day, the king went to the room where the queen's lover was.

00:55:11.796 --> 00:55:17.040
He killed him with his sword and threw the body down a deep well.

00:55:17.100 --> 00:55:20.231
Then he lay down on the sofa.

00:55:20.291 --> 00:55:23.411
Soon, the queen arrived.

00:55:23.471 --> 00:55:28.432
She went to her husband and beat him one hundred times.

00:55:28.493 --> 00:55:32.323
After that, she went to her lover's room.

00:55:32.383 --> 00:55:37.504
It was dark, so she couldn't see the man on the sofa very well.

00:55:37.564 --> 00:55:40.065
How are you today, my love?

00:55:40.125 --> 00:55:41.332
She said.

00:55:41.392 --> 00:55:43.099
Speak to me.

00:55:43.159 --> 00:55:45.020
The king answered.

00:55:45.080 --> 00:55:46.781
I'm very tired.

00:55:46.841 --> 00:55:52.544
When you beat your husband, he shouts very loudly, and I can't sleep.

00:55:52.604 --> 00:55:54.986
Take the spell off.

00:55:55.046 --> 00:55:57.798
I don't want to hear him anymore.

00:55:57.858 --> 00:56:01.990
The queen was very happy to hear her lover's voice again.

00:56:02.051 --> 00:56:06.254
She said, I'll take the spell off immediately, my love.

00:56:06.314 --> 00:56:12.018
She went back to her husband's room and took a cup of water which she heated on a fire.

00:56:12.078 --> 00:56:17.943
Then she said some magic words and threw the water over the block of marble.

00:56:18.003 --> 00:56:19.654
Now you are free.

00:56:19.714 --> 00:56:20.545
She said.

00:56:20.605 --> 00:56:23.667
Go away from here and never come back.

00:56:23.727 --> 00:56:29.741
The young king jumped for joy and the queen went back to her lover's room.

00:56:29.802 --> 00:56:31.923
My husband is free.

00:56:31.983 --> 00:56:32.954
She said.

00:56:33.014 --> 00:56:35.235
Are you better now, my love?

00:56:35.295 --> 00:56:39.368
The king answered, I'm still tired.

00:56:39.428 --> 00:56:47.402
Every night at midnight the fish in the lake jump out of the water and cry and shout loudly, I can't sleep.

00:56:47.462 --> 00:56:49.264
Take the spell off.

00:56:49.324 --> 00:56:51.726
I don't want to hear them anymore.

00:56:51.786 --> 00:56:56.898
The queen immediately ran to the lake and took the spell off.

00:56:56.958 --> 00:57:02.783
The fish became men, women and children again, and the lake became a city.

00:57:02.843 --> 00:57:08.846
The queen went back to her lover's room and said, The people are free.

00:57:08.906 --> 00:57:11.066
Do you feel better now?

00:57:11.127 --> 00:57:14.068
Come here, said the king.

00:57:14.128 --> 00:57:16.398
Come closer.

00:57:16.458 --> 00:57:18.989
The queen moved closer.

00:57:19.049 --> 00:57:25.132
Then the king suddenly jumped up and cut her body in half with his sword.

00:57:25.192 --> 00:57:26.636
The queen is dead.

00:57:26.696 --> 00:57:28.229
He said to the young king.

00:57:28.289 --> 00:57:31.120
And your city and your people are free.

00:57:31.180 --> 00:57:33.970
The young king was very happy.

00:57:34.031 --> 00:57:37.121
Why don't you come back with me to my country?

00:57:37.181 --> 00:57:38.331
Ask the king.

00:57:38.391 --> 00:57:40.232
I have no children of my own.

00:57:40.292 --> 00:57:43.652
You can be my son and rule my kingdom when I die.

00:57:43.712 --> 00:57:45.313
Thank you, I will.

00:57:45.373 --> 00:57:47.683
Replied the young king immediately.

00:57:47.743 --> 00:57:49.754
I never want to leave you.

00:57:49.814 --> 00:57:52.314
Good, said the king.

00:57:52.374 --> 00:57:55.620
I'll send my vizier to the Black Islands.

00:57:55.680 --> 00:57:58.297
He'll be a good Sultan.

00:57:58.357 --> 00:58:05.232
So the two kings made preparations for their long journey back to the king's country.

00:58:05.292 --> 00:58:11.758
They arrived safely, and they both lived peacefully for the rest of their lives.

